INT. CIRCUS WINTER QUARTERS - REHEARSAL BARN - MORNING

A drafty barn smelling of sawdust and horse. Trapezes hang at rest. A faded banner: "THE FLYING FONTAINES - SINCE 1923."

RINGMASTER BARNABY FONTAINE (60s, top hat, a tailcoat patched at the elbows) stands center ring, clipboard in hand. Beside him, the clown PICKLES (40s, half makeup, full despair) hangs his head. Atop a ladder, the aerialist VIOLETTA "VIVI" MORETTI (30s, sequined leotard under a parka) adjusts a rope. Below her, the strongman GUSTAV BERGSTROM (40s, shaved head, shoulders like a door) lifts a barbell without effort. And in a folding chair, the bookkeeper FANNY LU (50s, cardigan, adding machine) taps keys.

BARNABY
Ladies and gentlemen, we are bankrupt.

PICKLES
Again?

FANNY
Still.

VIVI
(from the ladder)
Barnaby, we've been bankrupt since Easter.

BARNABY
Since Easter, Vivi, we have been merely poor. Today we are bankrupt.

GUSTAV
I thought bankrupt meant we get a bailout.

FANNY
It means we get a lawyer.

PICKLES
I can juggle lawyers.

BARNABY
Pickles, you are not helping.

PICKLES
I am a clown. I am helping by being unhelpful.

VIVI
(sliding down the rope)
We could sell the elephant.

GUSTAV
We don't have an elephant.

VIVI
We have a very large dog.

FANNY
We have a very large debt.

BARNABY
I will not sell Cornelius.

PICKLES
Cornelius is a dog?

BARNABY
Cornelius is a lion.

GUSTAV
Cornelius is an old man in a lion costume.

BARNABY
Cornelius is our dignity.

A silence. Then the barn door bangs open and a gust of wind sweeps in. A figure steps through: a stranger in a pinstriped suit, briefcase in hand. MR. ALISTAIR PEMBERTON-HOYT (50s, banker's frown, a small gold pin on his lapel).

ALISTAIR
Good morning. I'm looking for Mr. Fontaine.

BARNABY
(stiffly)
You've found him.

ALISTAIR
I represent the Third Mutual Bank.

PICKLES
(to himself)
Here come the clowns.

ALISTAIR
I'm here to inspect the assets.

BARNABY
We have no assets.

ALISTAIR
Then I'm here to inspect the liabilities.

VIVI
(softly)
That's us.

Alistair opens his briefcase and pulls out a document. Fanny takes it. Reads. Her brows climb.

FANNY
(slowly)
Barnaby, this says the bank will forgive the debt.

BARNABY
It says what?

FANNY
On one condition.

ALISTAIR
That you perform.

GUSTAV
Perform?

ALISTAIR
My daughter's birthday party. Saturday. She's seven. She adores clowns.

Pickles raises one weary hand.

PICKLES
^I'm a clown.

BARNABY
^We are the Flying Fontaines.

ALISTAIR
Then it's settled.

Barnaby stares at the contract. At Alistair. At the faded banner.

BARNABY
Mr. Pemberton-Hoyt, we will not merely perform. We will astonish.

ALISTAIR
I merely require competence.

BARNABY
Competence is the death of art.

Fanny stamps the document. Gustav drops the barbell. Vivi whoops. Pickles produces, from nowhere, a handful of confetti and throws it into the air.

ALISTAIR
(dryly)
I'll see you Saturday.

He exits. The door bangs behind him.

FANNY
Barnaby, we have four days.

BARNABY
Then we shall rehearse for three and panic for one.

GUSTAV
Which day is panic?

BARNABY
Saturday, Gustav. Always Saturday.
